{"uid":"estorides_core/aviation.py","name":"aviation.py","qualname":"estorides_core/aviation.py","kind":"module","file":"estorides_core/aviation.py","line":1,"end_line":554,"language":"py","signature":"","params":[],"returns":"","decorators":[],"bases":[],"modifiers":[],"visibility":"public","doc":{"summary":"estorides_core.aviation ======================= Pure aircraft-intelligence helpers shared by the aerospace sources and the real-time map feeds.","description":"Everything here is deterministic and side-effect free: no network, no\nfilesystem, no environment. Transport lives in\n:mod:`estorides_core.feeds`; the orbital math lives in\n:mod:`estorides_core.aerospace`; the airport dataset lives in\n:mod:`estorides_core.airports`.\n\nWhat this module answers for one airframe:\n\n  * **Which class of aircraft is it?** — ICAO type designators and\n    ADS-B emitter categories collapse into a small display vocabulary\n    (light, turboprop, airliner, widebody, quadjet, helicopter, fastjet,\n    bizjet, glider, balloon, uav, ground, space).\n  * **Is it broadcasting an emergency?** — Mode A squawks 7500/7600/7700\n    plus the ADS-B emergency/priority field, with severity and the exact\n    wording an analyst may safely quote.\n  * **What do the community database flags say?** — military, interesting,\n    PIA and LADD bits from the readsb ``dbFlags`` bitfield.\n  * **How far apart are two points?** — haversine distance and\n    bounding-box helpers used by the regional aircraft feed.\n\nDesign note: nothing here decides that an incident happened. A squawk is\nwhat a transponder broadcast in one poll; crews pass through 7x00 codes\nwhile dialling, and a code does not confirm or resolve an emergency.\n\nBranding: Estorides, developed by Lazy Own Red Team.","params":[],"returns":null,"yields":null,"raises":[],"attributes":[],"examples":[],"notes":[],"see_also":[],"deprecated":"","since":"","style":"plain"},"parent":"","members":["estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_LIGHT","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_GLIDER","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_BALLOON","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_TURBOPROP","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_AIRLINER","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_WIDEBODY","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_QUADJET","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_HELICOPTER","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_FASTJET","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_BIZJET","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_UAV","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_GROUND","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_SPACE","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_UNKNOWN","estorides_core/aviation.py::CLASS_LABELS","estorides_core/aviation.py::EARTH_RADIUS_KM","estorides_core/aviation.py::KM_PER_NM","estorides_core/aviation.py::MAX_REGIONAL_RADIUS_NM","estorides_core/aviation.py::normalize_type_code","estorides_core/aviation.py::classify_aircraft","estorides_core/aviation.py::aircraft_class_label","estorides_core/aviation.py::EMERGENCY_KINDS","estorides_core/aviation.py::normalize_squawk","estorides_core/aviation.py::emergency_status","estorides_core/aviation.py::is_emergency","estorides_core/aviation.py::emergency_phrase","estorides_core/aviation.py::decode_db_flags","estorides_core/aviation.py::NAV_LEVELS","estorides_core/aviation.py::navigation_integrity","estorides_core/aviation.py::haversine_km","estorides_core/aviation.py::bbox_center_radius","estorides_core/aviation.py::point_in_bbox","estorides_core/aviation.py::normalize_hexdb_aircraft","estorides_core/aviation.py::normalize_hexdb_route"],"inferred_raises":[],"returns_value":null,"value":"","base_uids":[],"subclasses":[],"calls":[],"called_by":[]}
